        "    // Axis labels\n",
        "    ctx.fillStyle = \"#333\";\n",
        "    ctx.font = \"14px sans-serif\";\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.fillText(\"Linear predictor, z\", 310, 405);\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.save();\n",
        "    ctx.translate(22, 235);\n",
        "    ctx.rotate(-Math.PI / 2);\n",
        "    ctx.fillText(\"Predicted probability\", 0, 0);\n",
        "    ctx.restore();\n",
        "\n",
        "    // X ticks\n",
        "    const xTicks = [-10, -5, 0, 5, 10];\n",
        "\n",
        "    xTicks.forEach(function(tick){\n",
        "        const px = xScale(tick);\n",
        "\n",
        "        ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "        ctx.moveTo(px, bottom);\n",
        "        ctx.lineTo(px, bottom + 6);\n",
        "        ctx.stroke();\n",
        "\n",
        "        ctx.fillText(tick.toString(), px - 10, bottom + 24);\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Y ticks\n",
        "    const yTicks = [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1];\n",
        "\n",
        "    yTicks.forEach(function(tick){\n",
        "        const py = yScale(tick);\n",
        "\n",
        "        ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "        ctx.moveTo(left - 6, py);\n",
        "        ctx.lineTo(left, py);\n",
        "        ctx.stroke();\n",
        "\n",
        "        ctx.fillText(tick.toFixed(2), left - 52, py + 5);\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Reference line at probability 0.5\n",
        "    ctx.strokeStyle = \"#999\";\n",
        "    ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n",
        "    ctx.setLineDash([5,5]);\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "    ctx.moveTo(left, yScale(0.5));\n",
        "    ctx.lineTo(right, yScale(0.5));\n",
        "    ctx.stroke();\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.setLineDash([]);\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Sigmoid curve\n",
        "    ctx.strokeStyle = \"#2C7FB8\";\n",
        "    ctx.lineWidth = 3;\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "\n",
        "    for(let i=0; i<=200; i++){\n",
        "\n",
        "        const x =\n",
        "            xMin + (xMax - xMin) * i / 200;\n",
        "\n",
        "        const y =\n",
        "            sigmoid(x);\n",
        "\n",
        "        const px =\n",
        "            xScale(x);\n",
        "\n",
        "        const py =\n",
        "            yScale(y);\n",
        "\n",
        "        if(i === 0){\n",
        "            ctx.moveTo(px, py);\n",
        "        } else {\n",
        "            ctx.lineTo(px, py);\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.stroke();\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Current point\n",
        "    ctx.fillStyle = \"#D62728\";\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "    ctx.arc(\n",
        "        xScale(z),\n",
        "        yScale(p),\n",
        "        6,\n",
        "        0,\n",
        "        2*Math.PI\n",
        "    );\n",
        "    ctx.fill();\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Guide lines\n",
        "    ctx.strokeStyle = \"#D62728\";\n",
        "    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;\n",
        "    ctx.setLineDash([4,4]);\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "    ctx.moveTo(xScale(z), bottom);\n",
        "    ctx.lineTo(xScale(z), yScale(p));\n",
        "    ctx.stroke();\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.beginPath();\n",
        "    ctx.moveTo(left, yScale(p));\n",
        "    ctx.lineTo(xScale(z), yScale(p));\n",
        "    ctx.stroke();\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.setLineDash([]);\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Equation label\n",
        "    ctx.fillStyle = \"#333\";\n",
        "    ctx.font = \"16px sans-serif\";\n",
        "\n",
        "    ctx.fillText(\n",
        "        \"P(Y = 1) = 1 / (1 + e^(-z))\",\n",
        "        390,\n",
        "        60\n",
        "    );\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "document.getElementById(\"zSlider\")\n",
        "    .addEventListener(\n",
        "        \"input\",\n",
        "        drawSigmoid\n",
        "    );\n",
        "\n",
        "drawSigmoid();\n",
        "\n",
        "</script>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip title=\"What to Notice\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "- When $z = 0$, the predicted probability is 0.5.\n",
        "- Large positive values of $z$ produce probabilities close to 1.\n",
        "- Large negative values of $z$ produce probabilities close to 0.\n",
        "- The sigmoid function ensures that logistic regression outputs valid probabilities.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Cleveland Example\n",
        "\n",
        "We can predict the probability of heart disease using:\n",
        "\n",
        "- age;\n",
        "- cholesterol;\n",
        "- resting blood pressure;\n",
        "- maximum heart rate."
      ],
      "id": "3b1e250e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "\n",
        "X = df[[\"age\", \"chol\", \"trestbps\", \"thalach\"]]\n",
        "y = df[\"heart_disease\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "log_model = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
        "\n",
        "log_model.fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "predicted_probabilities = (\n",
        "    log_model\n",
        "    .predict_proba(X)[:,1]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "predicted_probabilities[:10]"
      ],
      "id": "a3d43d48",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The output is a probability.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "0.82\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "means an estimated 82% probability of heart disease.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Evaluating Logistic Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "For logistic regression, we are interested in how well the model distinguishes between patients with and without disease.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two commonly used metrics are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Accuracy**: proportion of correct predictions.\n",
        "- **Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC)**: measures how well the model separates the two classes across all decision thresholds."
      ],
      "id": "2fdd09df"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    accuracy_score,\n",
        "    roc_auc_score\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "predicted_labels = log_model.predict(X)\n",
        "\n",
        "accuracy = accuracy_score(\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    predicted_labels\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "auc = roc_auc_score(\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    predicted_probabilities\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Accuracy = {accuracy:.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"AUC = {auc:.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "4f3c8b81",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
